course: dictionary
lesson: 2117
title: Convention
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A convention is the usual or accepted way of doing something, a custom or rule that most people agree to follow. Capital letters at the start of sentences are English writing conventions. In maths, doing multiplication before addition is a convention that everyone agrees to use.
explain: Convention has other meanings too. «Henri Dunant helped start the Red Cross in 1863, and in 1864 countries signed the first Geneva Convention to protect wounded soldiers.» Here a convention is an official agreement between countries. A comic convention is a big meeting of people who share the same interest.
explain: Use the clues around the word. In «The UN Convention on the Rights of the Child, an agreement made by the countries of the world at the United Nations...», the words agreement made by countries show which meaning fits. Ask yourself: is it a custom, a meeting, or an agreement? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: A convention can be the usual or accepted way of doing something, such as a custom or rule.
fact: A convention can be a large meeting of people with the same interest or job, such as a comic convention.
fact: A convention can be an official agreement between countries, such as the Geneva Convention.
fact: In maths and writing, a convention is a standard rule everyone agrees to use, such as writing numbers left to right.
fact: «By convention» means following the usual accepted way, and «break with convention» means doing something differently.
exercise: «In 1864 countries signed the first Geneva Convention to protect wounded soldiers.» What is a convention here? | A large meeting of comic fans | *An official agreement between countries | A kind of party | A usual way of writing numbers
exercise: Maths has conventions. Which one is an example? | Drawing pictures of sums | Using only the number seven | *Writing numbers left to right, as everyone agrees to do | Singing the answer aloud
exercise: Lily says a comic convention is a fancy dinner. What is a comic convention? | A kind of agreement between countries | Rules about writing | *A big meeting of people who share an interest in comics | A type of school test
test: «The artist chose to break with convention and paint with her feet.» What does break with convention mean? | *Do something differently from the usual way | Hold a big meeting of artists | Follow the usual rules exactly | Sign an official agreement
test: «The UN Convention on the Rights of the Child lists the rights of every child.» What kind of convention is this? | A large fan meeting | *An official agreement made by countries | A usual custom at school | A standard maths rule
exam: Which sentence uses convention to mean a usual way of doing something? | The UN Convention was agreed in 1989 | The Geneva Convention protected wounded soldiers | The comic convention had ten thousand fans | *Starting sentences with a capital letter is a convention of English writing
